35,2,1,talk,Midori,,"I've found some concerning patterns. Previous joint clinics failed because neither department wanted to own the budget or rota, and external data agreements are taking over a year to finalize. We must avoid programs relying on fragile partnerships.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"My findings are a mix of hope and caution. The call-back trial significantly reduced readmissions for elderly patients, but the benefit vanished once it stopped. Conversely, the shared nursing round suffered from high failure rates due to external factors.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is precarious. We have nine unfilled ward nursing posts and a growing reliance on expensive agency cover. However, the midwifery rota currently has unusual slack due to falling birth numbers. We cannot add pressure to the wards.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The financial outlook is bleak. Our development allocation has dropped by nearly a quarter, and we're now paying for floor space from that same shrinking pot. We cannot afford a program that doesn't generate immediate, on-site revenue.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"My heart sinks a little to hear this. I found that our car park fills by eleven and rooms are quite full. Also, our booking system misses so much work; we are busier than we even realize.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, @Misaki, it seems we are all seeing the same fragility. If we choose a program that relies on outside surgeries or shared departmental rotas, it will likely collapse just like the previous clinic did. We need something self-contained.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion"",""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Midori, I agree. The call-back trial proved that targeted interventions work, but only if they are sustained. We must ensure the chosen program is not just a temporary experiment, but a permanent, integrated part of our care.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, sustainability is impossible if we ignore the staff. With the ward nursing shortage and agency costs rising, any program adding to their load is a risk. We should look for something that utilizes the slack in midwifery.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, utilizing slack is logical, but only if it's profitable. @Shizue mentioned the booking system is failing; we're losing revenue. Any program must be on-site to secure regional tariffs, or we're simply paying to provide free care.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Misaki"",""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I worry that bringing more people on-site for revenue might just lead to more chaos. If the car park is already full by eleven, where will these new patients go? We must be careful not to seize up.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shizue, you're right. If we can't park or find rooms, the program fails regardless of the budget. We need a solution that is self-contained, doesn't burden the wards, and avoids complex external agreements. Does such a balance exist?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"It may be difficult, but we must prioritize evidence of patient benefit. If we can find a program that targets high-risk groups—like the elderly in the call-back trial—without overloading the wards, we can achieve real impact.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"@Jonathan, I agree on the impact, but we must be realistic. If we ignore the staffing gaps, the ""impact"" will be a burnt-out team. We should prioritize programs that can be absorbed by the midwifery slack.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Misaki, focusing on midwifery slack is a start, but it's a narrow view. We are facing a twenty-five percent budget cut. If a program doesn't bill at the standard outpatient rate on-site, it's a liability, not an asset.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shion, I understand the need for money, but we must be gentle with our limits. If we push for more on-site revenue while the rooms are full and the parking is gone, we may only create frustration for everyone.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"It seems we are caught between financial necessity and operational reality. We must find a candidate that is self-sufficient, avoids external bureaucracy, and doesn't overload our already strained ward staff or physical space. Let's be very cautious.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I agree. We must avoid the cycle of starting initiatives only to let them fade. Let us look for a candidate that offers proven patient benefits while remaining mindful of our staffing and space constraints.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a program that is sustainable for the people, not just the budget. Let's see if any of the candidates can be managed by the midwifery team to avoid further ward burnout.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's stop pretending that ""sustainability"" is just about staff happiness. Without a positive tariff return and a realistic budget, there is no program to sustain. I'll be voting for the most financially viable, on-site option.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I hope we can all find a middle ground. Let us look at the candidates with kindness, but also with a clear eye for whether our poor building can actually hold them. I shall see you in the final round.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
